


   =====( AddSysop V1.00 )============================================


        Trion AddSysop Utility.

        (c) Copyright Paul Spijkerman, '94-'97. All rights reserved.

        Written for use with the Trion BBS package.


   ===================================================================


   Addsysop is a little programm to add a user with sysop level
   to the Userdatabase.

   When you setup the BBS for the first time you probably
   want to add yourself as a sysop to the userbase.
   This utility can be used add installation to add your name,
   but if you already logged in once it can't be used.
   This utility was made to be integrated in an install script
   but nothing useable or practicall has materialized yet.


   Note that you don't need AddSysop if you want to add a
   sysop ... you can simply log in and change the level
   of this person with the editor under the F8 key.
   Or if the user already exists you could use the 
   offline GUI usereditor or the online Usereditor.

   You probably want to login with the 'Sysop login'
   button in the BBS GUI .. note that you have to change
   the sysop name in the 'trion:cfg/trion-X.cfg' or
   else it will use the default name instead of yours.


   You use this programm by typing:

   AddSysop  "Name"  "Password"

   Note that TrionRM must be not running.
   Note that the "" are only necessay if there are spaces
   in the name or password.


